{
 "id": "settlement-root-v1",
 "description": "Grown-root EXTERIOR settlement kit \u2014 the canopy/trunk building culture the catalogue's `hist-grove-capital` and 34 other records assume (audit \u00a74 claim `grown-root-architecture`). Pure packaging of BM&V's Bosmer tree-city (`citebosmer`) as its authors built it: the three trunk-house forms with their own balcony, door, window and liana pieces (`tronc` = trunk house, `champ` = tapered mushroom-cap house, `gland` = hanging acorn/pod house), the COMPLETE modular elevated walkway system (all 52 `passerelles/troncons` straights, climbs, turns, 45/90 curves, T/X/Y junctions, stair and end pieces) and its `kiosque` platform family (deck, side walls, railings, access ramps, fixation collar), plus the giant host trees and root base the houses are authored to hang from. Extended with HTBM Cipactli Hist roots and ramp for the ground layer, and Mud Mother Grove's Argonian lanterns, totem, bone chime, banner, woven fences, plank bridge and platforms so the settlement reads Argonian rather than Bosmer. Interiors for these dwellings come from dungeon-root-v1 (`dwelling`/`civic-hall` interior families also resolve there). NOT tropicalised: no vanilla-backed piece is present. EXCLUDED: `housetroncbalcon001` \u2014 it carries no exportable geometry (an editor marker/parent node); the usable trunk balcony is `housetroncbalcon15v001` with its `acces15d/i` approach and `endl/endr` caps.",
 "culture": "argonian-root",
 "output": "tooling/asset-pipeline/output/kits/settlement-root-v1.glb",
