  0.35,
  0.12
 ],
 "textureMaxSize": 512,
 "snapLogic": {
  "passerelles": "The walkway system's own encoded grid \u2014 this is the whole reason to package it intact. `passl<len>[h<rise>]<d|i>01`: `l` = length in Bethesda units (64/128/160/256/512), `h` = the rise that segment climbs (0/32/64/128), `d`/`i` = the two authored handrail sides (droite/interieur), which must stay consistent along a run or the rail flips. `passl256h64startd01` is the authored START of a climbing run. `passturn45...` are flat/climbing 45-degree turns (`ldi`/`rdi`/`lid`/`rid` encode which side turns and which rail leads); `passcirc45r1280...` and `passcirc90r448/r576...` are true arcs at a fixed radius (1280 / 448 / 576 units) \u2014 chain only arcs of the SAME radius. `passjunct`/`passjuncx`/`passjuncy` are the T, cross and Y junctions; `passend01` terminates; `passesc128h64d01` is the stair. All pieces butt end-to-end on the deck plane with origin at the entry face, so a run is a sum of `l` values and its height a sum of `h` values.",
  "kiosque": "A platform node dropped into a walkway run: `kiosk01` deck, `kioskaccesd01`/`kioskaccesi01` the two approach ramps that mate to a `pass...` end, `kioskbarriered01`/`kioskbarrierei01` the railings, `kioskmurd01`/`kioskmuri01` the solid sides, `kioskfixation001` the collar that ties it to a trunk.",
  "houses": "Each house form is a shell plus its OWN accessory family; do not cross forms. `housetronc001` takes `housetroncbalcon*` (with `acces15d/i` approach and `endl/endr` caps), `housetroncdooret/rc01` and `housetroncwindowet/rc00x`. `housechamp001` takes the `45v` balcony family, the `acceslat*` lateral accesses, `finl/finr` end caps and `housechampwindow00x`. `housegland001` hangs and takes `houseglandacceslatd/i01`, its own door and `windowet/rc` set. `housechamplianess001`/`lianestronc` and `housetronc001lianess` are the authored liana drops that visually tie a house to the tree.",
  "trees": "`treegiant01` is the host trunk, `treegiantbranche1-7/12/13` the boughs and `treegiantbrancheleaves01b/03/04` the foliage; `treegiantrootbase01` is the root flare at the base. Houses and walkways are hand-attached to boughs \u2014 there are no snap points, the branch geometry is the guide.",
  "unitScale": "Bethesda units; 0.0142240 m/unit. Measured extents in settlement-root-v1.kit.json."
 },
